---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy — {{brand}}"
  description="What cookies {{brand}} uses, why we use them, and how you can manage or withdraw your consent at any time."
>
  <div class="article-wrap"><div class="container">
    <article class="prose" style="max-width:760px;margin:0 auto">
      <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated: August 24, 2026</em></p>

      <div class="callout warn">
        <span class="c-label">Note</span>
        <p>This is a template and must be reviewed by a qualified lawyer and completed with your company details before publication.</p>
      </div>

      <p>This Cookie Policy explains how {{domain}} (the "Site") uses cookies and similar technologies. It should be read together with our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

      <h2>What is a cookie?</h2>
      <p>A cookie is a small text file placed on your device (computer, tablet or smartphone) when you visit a website. Cookies allow the site to recognise your device, remember your preferences and choices, measure audience, and — where you allow it — display and personalise advertising. Similar technologies (such as local storage, pixels and tags) may be used for comparable purposes; references to "cookies" in this policy include those technologies.</p>

      <h2>Categories of cookies we use</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Strictly necessary cookies:</strong> required for the Site to function (for example, to record your cookie consent choices or keep the Site secure). These do not require your consent and cannot be disabled through the consent banner.</li>
        <li><strong>Audience measurement (analytics) cookies:</strong> help us understand how visitors use the Site so we can improve it. They are set only where the law requires your consent.</li>
        <li><strong>Advertising and personalisation cookies:</strong> used by our advertising partners to serve ads, limit how often you see the same ad, measure ad performance and — with your consent — personalise the ads you see.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Third-party cookies</h2>
      <p>Some cookies are set by third parties, in particular:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google (AdSense and advertising partners):</strong> for serving, measuring and personalising ads. Learn more in <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google's overview of how it uses data</a> and <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google's advertising policies</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Analytics provider:</strong> [Analytics tool name, e.g. Google Analytics / Plausible].</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These third parties are responsible for their own cookies and processing, in accordance with their own privacy policies.</p>

      <h2>Cookies and technologies used</h2>
      <p>The table below lists the main cookies and similar technologies used on the Site. It is provided for transparency and is kept up to date; exact names and durations set by third parties may vary.</p>
      <table class="data-table" style="margin:12px 0">
        <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Provider</th><th>Category</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Duration</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td><strong>rp-consent</strong></td><td>{{brand}}</td><td>Strictly necessary</td><td>Stores your cookie consent choice</td><td>6 months</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>__Secure-ENID / NID</strong></td><td>Google</td><td>Advertising</td><td>Ad serving, frequency capping, preferences</td><td>up to 13 months</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>IDE / test_cookie</strong></td><td>Google (DoubleClick)</td><td>Advertising</td><td>Ad measurement and personalisation (with consent)</td><td>up to 13 months</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>[analytics cookie]</strong></td><td>[Analytics tool]</td><td>Audience measurement</td><td>Anonymous audience statistics</td><td>[e.g. 13 months]</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Advertising and analytics cookies are only set <strong>after you give consent</strong> via the banner (Google Consent Mode v2 default is "denied" until you accept).</p>

      <h2>Managing your consent</h2>
      <p>When you first visit the Site, a consent banner lets you accept all cookies, reject non-essential cookies, or set your preferences by category. Strictly necessary cookies are always active. We store a record of your choice so we do not ask again on every visit.</p>

      <h2>Withdrawing or changing your consent</h2>
      <p>You can change or withdraw your consent at any time by [reopening the cookie settings, e.g. via the "Cookie settings" link in the footer]. Withdrawing consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before you withdrew it.</p>

      <h2>Managing cookies in your browser</h2>
      <p>You can also block or delete cookies through your browser settings. Most browsers let you refuse cookies, delete existing ones, or notify you when a cookie is set. Please note that disabling certain cookies may affect how the Site works. Instructions are available for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://support.google.com/chrome/answer/95647" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Google Chrome</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.mozilla.org/kb/cookies-information-websites-store-on-your-computer" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Mozilla Firefox</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.apple.com/guide/safari/manage-cookies-sfri11471/mac" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Apple Safari</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://support.microsoft.com/help/4468242" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Microsoft Edge</a></li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Cookie lifetime</h2>
      <p>Cookies are either <strong>session cookies</strong> (deleted when you close your browser) or <strong>persistent cookies</strong> (which remain for a defined period). The lifetime of each cookie depends on its purpose and provider, and generally does not exceed [e.g. 13 months] for consent-based cookies. Consent records are kept for [e.g. 6 months].</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top of this page reflects the latest revision.</p>
    </article>
  </div></div>
</BaseLayout>
